{
 "Each word here is a point in space: three numbers. Words that are used in similar ways end up near each other.": "5798064d44.mp3",
 "Countries sit on the bottom floor, roughly where they are on the map. Capitals float one floor up, and national dishes two floors up.": "2f7060be3b.mp3",
 "The arrow from Nigeria up to Abuja means: the capital of. And it is almost the same arrow for every country.": "5aae391982.mp3",
 "So take Abuja, subtract Nigeria, add Kenya. Start the arrow at Kenya, follow it, and the nearest word is Nairobi.": "2684bed6fa.mp3",
 "It works for food. Egusi minus Nigeria plus Senegal lands on thieboudienne.": "7e8e7b370d.mp3",
 "We placed these words by hand so you can see them. A real model learns hundreds of numbers per word from billions of sentences, and these directions appear on their own.": "ed2ab2dd34.mp3"
